# The leftover test labels of the old short name, and the check that keeps
# them out: `cargo xtask rename --check`.

[break] an-upper-case-label-passes-the-check
rule: A label of capitals built on the old alias (an environment variable of a test, with or without an underscore) fails the check.
file: xtask/src/rename.rs
in: is_label
find: byte == b'_' || (byte.is_ascii_uppercase() && byte != b'X')
replace: byte == b'_'
caught-by:
    rename::tests::the_check_finds_a_label_built_on_the_old_alias

[break] a-lower-case-label-passes-the-check
rule: A mark, a name or a scratch name built on the old alias (a test kit role's mark, a quoted name) fails the check.
file: xtask/src/rename.rs
in: is_label
find: byte.is_ascii_lowercase() && byte != b'x'
replace: byte == b'#'
caught-by:
    rename::tests::the_check_finds_a_label_built_on_the_old_alias

[break] the-variable-as-cx-passes-the-check
rule: The variable that means "run as the alias" fails the check.
file: xtask/src/rename.rs
in: is_label
find: && word_start
replace: && !word_start
caught-by:
    rename::tests::the_check_finds_a_label_built_on_the_old_alias

[break] cxx-is-a-label
rule: The C++ extension and its lower-case names are not labels of the old alias.
file: xtask/src/rename.rs
in: is_label
find: && byte != b'x'
replace: && true
caught-by:
    rename::tests::words_that_only_look_like_a_label_are_not_one

[break] upper-case-cxx-is-a-label
rule: The compiler's variables (the C++ compiler's name and its flags) are not labels of the old alias.
file: xtask/src/rename.rs
in: is_label
find: && byte != b'X'
replace: && true
caught-by:
    rename::tests::words_that_only_look_like_a_label_are_not_one

[break] the-middle-of-a-word-is-a-label
rule: The two capitals inside a longer word (a session id) are not a label.
file: xtask/src/rename.rs
in: is_label
find: .is_some_and(|before| is_word_byte(bytes[before]))
replace: .is_some_and(|before| !is_word_byte(bytes[before]) && false)
caught-by:
    rename::tests::words_that_only_look_like_a_label_are_not_one

[break] the-check-ignores-labels
rule: The check reports a label on its line, not only the old names and the alias.
file: xtask/src/rename.rs
in: violations
find: for at in label_positions(text) {
replace: for at in label_positions(text).into_iter().take(0) {
caught-by:
    rename::tests::the_check_finds_a_label_built_on_the_old_alias
